<script>
const TEST_QUESTIONS = [
  {
    num: 1,
    instruction: 'Read the information and answer the question.',
    imgSide: '<img src="test1/q1.jpg" alt="Newton"><div class="q-passage" style="margin-top:10px"><p>Newton was a brilliant physicist and mathematician. He loved difficult problems. One day, he invited a guest for dinner, but he stayed in his room to work on an equation. He was so focused on his study that he completely forgot his guest and his meal. This behavior shows his absent-minded personality.</p></div>',
    question: 'Which of the following is CORRECT according to the text?',
    options: [
      'Newton preferred spending time with his visitors over science.',
      'He had a very organized daily routine and never forgot a meal.',
      'His passion for solving problems sometimes made him forgetful.',
      'He found it impossible to focus on a single study for a long time.'
    ],
    ans: 'C'
  },
  {
    num: 2,
    instruction: 'Read the text and answer the question.',
    imgSide: '<img src="test1/q2.jpg" alt="Microchip lab"><div class="q-passage" style="margin-top:10px"><p>Scientific achievements improve our lives in many ways. In 1958, Jack Kilby invented the microchip. This achievement allowed scientists to produce smaller and faster computers. Before this invention, computers were massive and they occupied large rooms. In the 1970s, computers became cheaper, so people began to use them in their houses.</p></div>',
    question: 'What was the primary effect of the invention of the microchip?',
    options: [
      'It made computers more expensive and difficult to find.',
      'It enabled the production of more compact and efficient devices.',
      'It stopped people from using computers for simple calculations.',
      'It allowed people to use room-sized computers at their homes.'
    ],
    ans: 'B'
  },
  {
    num: 3,
    instruction: 'Read the speech bubbles and answer the question.',
    imgSide: '<div class="q-passage"><p><strong>Şefika:</strong> I admire Marie Curie because she worked under dangerous conditions to discover radium.</p><p><strong>Kaan:</strong> I think scientific systematic observations are essential to understand nature.</p><p><strong>Eylül:</strong> Currently, my sister is in the school lab. She is conducting an experiment.</p><p><strong>Akif:</strong> I want to find the meaning of "milestone" in my science textbook.</p></div>',
    question: 'Who is talking about a current action in a specific place?',
    options: ['Şefika', 'Kaan', 'Eylül', 'Akif'],
    ans: 'C'
  },
  {
    num: 4,
    instruction: 'Read the definitions and find the ODD one.',
    imgSide: '<div class="q-passage"><p><strong>Exploration:</strong> Traveling through an unknown area to learn about it.</p><p><strong>Genius:</strong> A person with exceptional intelligence or creative power.</p><p><strong>Vaccination:</strong> A way to protect people against serious diseases.</p><p><strong>Orbit:</strong> The curved path of a planet around a star or a moon.</p></div>',
    question: 'Which of the following is NOT a field of science according to the definitions above?',
    options: ['Astronomy', 'Biology', 'Geography', 'Law'],
    ans: 'D'
  },
  {
